<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Purge (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>purge
purge &lt;someone or something&gt;
</pre>
<p><b>purge</b> alone cleans the room: every monster and every thing that can 
be picked up is destroyed, in scorching flames. Players, things fixed in 
place, and players' corpses are spared.
</p><p><b>purge &lt;name&gt;</b> disintegrates one monster, thing or player in the room 
(only here: name something you can see). A corpse is destroyed with 
everything in it, and its saved copy deleted, so it won't come back after 
a reboot. Purging a player takes level 245, and 
only works on players of a lower level than yours: it removes them from 
the game at once.
</p><p>Rooms can't be purged. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Load</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Corpses</a>
</pre>




</div>